## 3. Third-party runtimes bundled by the installers

These components are **not committed to this repository** — they were removed
from it deliberately, and the build fetches them. They are listed here because
the installers redistribute them, and the licence obligations travel with the
installer.

| Component | Licence | Note |
|---|---|---|
| **ONLYOFFICE Document Builder** | **AGPL-3.0** | Used for document conversion. Same network-copyleft reasoning as §2.1, and the most significant item of this section. |
| **Azul Zulu JRE 25** | GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception | A complete Java runtime. The Classpath Exception is what makes bundling it workable; the GPL-2.0 source-offer obligation still applies to the runtime itself. |
| **LanguageTool** and its dictionaries | LGPL-2.1, GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, MPL, CC-BY-SA-4.0, Apache-2.0, BSD, MIT — mixed | Upstream ships per-component licence files under `third-party-licenses/`. No aggregated inventory exists upstream; building one is an open task. |
| **Tectonic** | MIT | TeX engine. Bundles TeX Live resources with their own licences. |
| **DocxToHtml** | project-owned | Sources are in `bin/DocxToHtml/`; only the compiled output is absent. |
| **pdf.js** | Apache-2.0 | Vendored under `src/renderer/pdfjs/`, including Foxit and Liberation fonts and Adobe CMap data, each under its own terms. |
| **CanvasKit / Skia** | BSD-3-Clause | Vendored as `src/renderer/canvaskit/canvaskit.wasm`. |
| **Fluent UI System Icons** | MIT | Vendored SVG set, by Microsoft. |
| **Croscore fonts** (Arimo, Tinos, Carlito) | Apache-2.0 / SIL OFL | Vendored under `src/renderer/public/fonts/`. |

**Open task:** this section is an inventory, not a compliance package. Shipping
an installer that redistributes GPL and AGPL components requires making the
corresponding source available to recipients. That mechanism does not exist
yet.

